  "id": "Compound::DB01438 - Gene::6323",
  "verbalization": "Phenazopyridine is likely to interact with Scn1a through a shared mechanism involving voltage-gated sodium channels. The evidence suggests that Phenazopyridine binds to multiple subunits of voltage-gated sodium channels, specifically Scn11a, Scn8a, and Scn2a, all of which participate in voltage-gated sodium channel activity. This indicates that Phenazopyridine may modulate sodium channel function by binding to these subunits, potentially influencing the electrical activity of neurons. The consistent involvement of Scn1a in the activity of these channels suggests that Phenazopyridine could exert its effects through a common pathway, possibly by stabilizing or altering the function of these channels. The overlapping roles of these subunits in the same biological process support the idea that Phenazopyridine may act on a broader network of sodium channels, contributing to a unified mechanism of action.",
